build/
build-*/
*.o
*.so
*.a

# CAModel / device run artifacts, written into the CURRENT WORKING DIRECTORY by
# the simulator and the profiler rather than into the build tree, so a runner
# invoked from the repository root leaves them here. One CAModel run of the
# decode drops a dump per log per vector and cube subcore per AI Core -- 423
# files and ~20 MB each for the instruction logs at 32 cores -- which buries
# `git status` and is one `git add -A` away from being committed.
#
# They are evidence, and the README is explicit that a PASS line is not to be
# read without auditing the trace. Ignoring them is about not versioning them:
# keep the ones that matter somewhere outside the working tree, or run from a
# scratch directory.
*.dump
profile_*_log*.toml

# Generated golden dumps (golden/generate_dumps.py output): binary fixtures,
# regenerated on demand rather than versioned.
golden/dumps/

# Editor state.
.vscode/
